{
  "_readme": [
    "UI entry ledger, seeded at the 2026-11-15 refactor meeting (2458dec).",
    "check-ui-entries.py verifies every implemented platform row's anchor (file+regex) exists in source, so a feature cannot silently lose its entry; not-implemented rows must carry a note — no silent gaps.",
    "conform_b4: ok = row exists in UI_B4_PLAN §2/§5's decided structure; extension = feature added after B4, parking spot not yet decided by a meeting (docs/UIUX_REFACTOR_2026-11-15.md §9-1); violation = parked where B4 §2:61 forbids (the instrument sheet must not accumulate feature entries).",
    "anchors are source-level: a tag present in source is necessary but NOT sufficient (a chip inside a discarded closure carries a valid id — see pad-send on iOS). Runtime reachability belongs to UI tests; this ledger is the map, not the proof."
  ],
